  "question": {
    "text": "The compound used in the treatment of lead poisoning is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Desferrioxime B",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "EDTA",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Cis-platin",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>penicillamine",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> Sodium calcium edetate, a salt of EDTA (Ethylene Diamine Tetra-acetic Acid), is used to bind metals in the chelation&nbsp;therapy, such as for treating mercury and lead poisoning.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> Cis-platin is used as an anti-cancer drug.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math> penicillamine is used for treating copper poisoning.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> Desterrioxime B is used for treating iron poisoning."
  }
